   <conbody class="- topic/body  concept/conbody " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/operating_modes/predictive_learning.dita" xtrc="conbody:1;25:13">
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/operating_modes/predictive_learning.dita" xtrc="p:1;26:10">This section describes the predictive learning stage of the learning mode.</p>
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/operating_modes/predictive_learning.dita" xtrc="p:2;27:10">After the Quick Learning stage, OtoSense ™ enters the Predictive Learning stage, which takes approximately four weeks ￼. This stage enables improved predictions for all detectable fault types.</p>
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/operating_modes/predictive_learning.dita" xtrc="p:3;28:10">During this stage, faults will be predicted within the parameters of the motor conditions that the SMS observed during Quick Learning. The motor model will continue to improve based on learnings from any changes to operational conditions.</p>
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/operating_modes/predictive_learning.dita" xtrc="p:4;29:10">During the Predictive Learning stage, the status indicator on both the mobile and web application will show the motor status. For more information, see <xref href="#Figure3" class="- topic/xref " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/operating_modes/predictive_learning.dita" xtrc="xref:1;29:184">Figure 3</xref> and <xref href="#Figure4" class="- topic/xref " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/operating_modes/predictive_learning.dita" xtrc="xref:2;29:226">Figure 4</xref>.</p>
   </conbody>
</concept>